        <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>reinterpret_tag</computeroutput> returns a copy of an iterator and changes the type of the result&apos;s system tag. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Tag</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Any system tag. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Iterator</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Any iterator type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>iter</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The iterator of interest. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>An iterator of unspecified type whose system tag is <computeroutput>Tag</computeroutput> and whose behavior is otherwise equivalent to <computeroutput>iter</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Unlike <computeroutput>retag</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>reinterpret_tag</computeroutput> does not enforce that the converted-to system tag be related to the converted-from system tag. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para>retag </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
